    rdf:value """Tuesday, Dec. 22, 1908
New Willard Hotel, Washington.
Saw the St. Gaudens exhibit — didn’t care much for it. He over-uses drapery in sculpture as Andrea did in painting, only it’s real drapery, in stone, and futile and ugly.
Lunched with Henry Adams. There was a heavy snow-storm, so we stayed in the rest of the day. """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 379 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1908> .

